## The 5 Facts About the $32,290 Jump

The title of this guide promised five facts about the jump. Here they are in full.

**Fact 1: You are paying 196% more, not 50% more.**

Most buyers expect a 50% price premium for a 50% weight increase. The actual premium is 196%.

A 2ct G-VS2 GIA Excellent starts at $16,490. A 3ct G-VS2 starts at $48,780.

The dollar difference is $32,290 — not because jewelers mark up 3ct, but because the per-carat price at 3ct ($16,260/ct) is nearly double that at 2ct ($8,245/ct). Every carat in the 3ct stone is priced at 3ct rates.

**Fact 2: The 3ct per-carat rate is 1.97× the 2ct rate — on every carat.**

Diamond pricing is not progressive. When you buy a 3ct stone, all three carats are priced at the 3ct per-carat rate.

There is no "2ct rate on the first two carats." The 3ct per-carat rate is 97% higher than the 2ct rate, and you pay that rate across all three carats. This is The Luxury Jump Tax in mathematical form.

**Fact 3: The face-up area grows 35% — the price grows 196%.**

A 3ct round at 9.4mm has 35% more face-up area than a 2ct at 8.1mm. The price grows 196%.

That means the price grows 5.6× faster than the face-up area. Visual presence grows modestly while cost grows dramatically — a defining feature of the luxury tier.

**Fact 4: Natural 3ct inventory is thin — about 15 stones vs 67+ at 2ct.**

On Blue Nile, roughly 67 natural 2ct GIA Excellent round brilliants are available at any time. At 3ct, that falls to about 15.

Thinner inventory means less price competition. The specific combination of grades and proportions you want may simply not exist. This supply compression is itself a driver of The Luxury Jump Tax.

**Fact 5: A lab-grown 3ct D-VVS1 at $7,000 is $9,490 cheaper than a natural 2ct.**

A [lab-grown 3ct D-VVS1 IGI Ideal](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29116878?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) costs $7,000 and measures 9.4mm face-up. A [natural 2ct G-VS2](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29307739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) costs $16,490 at 8.1mm.

The lab 3ct is larger, better graded (D vs G, VVS1 vs VS2), and $9,490 cheaper. The Luxury Jump Tax does not exist in the lab market — where 3ct is routine, not rare.

